# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Without it, a clone on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` — which is the Git
# for Windows installer's own suggested setting, not a fringe configuration —
# checks every text file out with CRLF. That is invisible to `git status` and
# `git diff`, so a contributor who hits the consequences has no way to
# self-diagnose from the tools that would normally tell them.
#
# The consequences measured on a real clone:
#   - `generated-types-are-fresh` fails. The generator emits LF; the working
#     copy holds CRLF; the test compares bytes, so it reports the generated
#     types as stale when their content is byte-identical after normalisation.
#   - `bconnect-compliance-mcp`'s build prebuild check aborts before `tsc`
#     runs, which cascades into failing test files in two unrelated servers
#     because the gateway can no longer resolve the compliance package.
#
# A first clone that fails its own test suite for a reason the contributor
# cannot see is the worst possible first five minutes of an open-source
# project, and one line of configuration prevents it.

# Default: Git decides what is text, and text is LF in the repo and in the
# working tree. `eol=lf` rather than `eol=native` is deliberate — the generated
# types are compared byte-for-byte against a generator that emits LF, so a
# native checkout would reintroduce exactly the failure above.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF even on Windows checkouts: CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one place CRLF is the platform norm. These are Windows
# scripts run by Windows operators; keep them CRLF in the working tree.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.psd1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touched: any transformation corrupts these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
